{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSZuarLAZn9u1Jbv3iXp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rule picks levels from the instruction class (taken from the description), the case terms and the compared states.\n\n- **Units.** Cut units cannot be restored by refinement, so a unit is cut only where it seems clearly unneeded.\n  - **D-cache (`near_mem_dcache`):** cut, except for loads, stores and AMOs, where the mem sub-property or the loaded value needs it. With only ADDI fetched, its outputs feed no checked behaviour.\n  - **I-cache (`near_mem_icache`):** always kept. The fetched instruction and `imem_pc` come through it.\n  - **CSR register file (`csr_regfile`):** cut only for `xk.frame`. A spurious trap or interrupt never writes a GPR, so x_k still holds. Elsewhere it is kept, because a trap would redirect the pc or stop the write.\n- **GPRs.** Every register named by the case through an operand field (rs1 or rs2) is kept, because its start mapping is needed. For a write sub-property `rd==k`, x_k is \"word\" unless it is also a source; then it is \"keep\". In `xk.frame`, x_k is kept. Register x0 is kept when named or compared. For a `mem` sub-property with no case, the GPRs are kept only for JALR, loads, stores and AMOs, where pc or address states read rs1. All other GPRs are \"havoc\". Havoc is still the right default for registers no state reads, and a needed register would be restored by refinement.\n- **Operators.** All are kept. The adder holds no state, so \"uf\" saves no state bits. It also risks spurious counterexamples when the instruction executes after its start cycle.\n\n```python\nRV32I = [\"LUI\", \"AUIPC\", \"JAL\", \"JALR\", \"BEQ\", \"BNE\", \"BLT\", \"BGE\", \"BLTU\", \"BGEU\",\n         \"LB\", \"LH\", \"LW\", \"LBU\", \"LHU\", \"SB\", \"SH\", \"SW\",\n         \"ADDI\", \"SLTI\", \"SLTIU\", \"XORI\", \"ORI\", \"ANDI\", \"SLLI\", \"SRLI\", \"SRAI\",\n         \"ADD\", \"SUB\", \"SLL\", \"SLT\", \"SLTU\", \"XOR\", \"SRL\", \"SRA\", \"OR\", \"AND\",\n         \"FENCE\", \"ECALL\", \"EBREAK\"]\n\nLOADS = [\"LB\", \"LH\", \"LW\", \"LBU\", \"LHU\"]\nSTORES = [\"SB\", \"SH\", \"SW\"]\n\n\ndef tokens(text):\n    out = []\n    cur = \"\"\n    for ch in text:\n        if ch.isalnum() if hasattr(ch, \"isalnum\") else False:\n            cur = cur + ch\n        else:\n            if cur:\n                out.append(cur)\n            cur = \"\"\n    if cur:\n        out.append(cur)\n    return out\n\n\ndef is_alnum(ch):\n    return ch.isdigit() or (ch.lower() != ch.upper()) or ch == \"_\"\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    out = []\n    cur = \"\"\n    for ch in text:\n        if is_alnum(ch):\n            cur = cur + ch\n        else:\n            if cur:\n                out.append(cur)\n            cur = \"\"\n    if cur:\n        out.append(cur)\n    return out\n\n\ndef mnemonic(design):\n    desc = design.get(\"description\", \"\") or \"\"\n    lines = desc.split(\"\\n\")\n    # prefer the Benchmark line\n    for line in lines:\n        toks = tokenize(line)\n        if len(toks) > 0 and toks[0] == \"Benchmark\":\n            for t in toks:\n                if t.upper() == t and t in RV32I:\n                    return t\n    for t in tokenize(desc):\n        if t in RV32I:\n            return t\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef choose(sub, design):\n    instr = mnemonic(design)\n    is_mem_instr = (instr in LOADS) or (instr in STORES) or instr.startswith(\"AMO\")\n    operand_fields = design.get(\"operand_fields\", []) or []\n    states = sub.get(\"states\", []) or []\n    terms = sub.get(\"case_terms\", []) or []\n\n    rd_eq = None\n    rd_ne = None\n    src_regs = set()\n    for t in terms:\n        f = t.get(\"field\")\n        op = t.get(\"op\")\n        v = t.get(\"value\")\n        if f == \"rd\":\n            if op == \"==\":\n                rd_eq = v\n            else:\n                rd_ne = v\n        elif f in (\"rs1\", \"rs2\") and op == \"==\":\n            src_regs.add(int(v))\n\n    state_regs = set()\n    for s in states:\n        if len(s) > 1 and s[0] == \"x\" and s[1:].isdigit():\n            state_regs.add(int(s[1:]))\n\n    is_frame = rd_ne is not None and rd_eq is None\n    is_write = rd_eq is not None\n    no_case = len(terms) == 0\n\n    # Which operand fields are fixed by the case\n    fixed_fields = set([t.get(\"field\") for t in terms if t.get(\"op\") == \"==\"])\n    unfixed_operands = [f for f in operand_fields if f not in fixed_fields]\n\n    keep_all_gprs = False\n    if no_case and len(unfixed_operands) > 0:\n        # mem-like sub-property without operand split: keep GPRs only if\n        # non-register states may read source registers\n        non_x = [s for s in states if not (len(s) > 1 and s[0] == \"x\" and s[1:].isdigit())]\n        if len(non_x) > 0 and (instr == \"JALR\" or is_mem_instr or instr == \"\"):\n            keep_all_gprs = True\n    elif is_write and len(unfixed_operands) > 0:\n        keep_all_gprs = True\n    elif (not is_frame) and (not is_write) and len(unfixed_operands) > 0:\n        keep_all_gprs = True\n\n    result = {}\n    for c in design[\"choices\"]:\n        cid = c[\"id\"]\n        kind = c[\"kind\"]\n        levels = c[\"levels\"]\n        lvl = levels[0]\n        if kind == \"unit\":\n            inst = c.get(\"instance\", \"\")\n            parts = inst.split(\".\")\n            last = parts[-1] if len(parts) > 0 else inst\n            if last == \"dcache\":\n                lvl = \"keep\" if is_mem_instr else \"cut\"\n            elif last == \"icache\":\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif c.get(\"module\", \"\") == \"mkCSR_RegFile\":\n                lvl = \"cut\" if is_frame else \"keep\"\n            else:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n        elif kind == \"gpr\":\n            j = int(c.get(\"register\", -1))\n            if keep_all_gprs:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif j in src_regs:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif is_frame and j == rd_ne:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif is_write and j == rd_eq:\n                lvl = \"word\" if \"word\" in levels else \"keep\"\n            elif j in state_regs:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            else:\n                lvl = \"havoc\" if \"havoc\" in levels else \"keep\"\n        else:\n            lvl = \"keep\"\n        if lvl not in levels:\n            lvl = levels[0]\n        result[cid] = lvl\n    return result\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":24607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d432920-1915-43e6-8526-d00d08958206","uuid":"d5a666bc-f938-4fa7-800a-141b7efb2769","timestamp":"2026-10-27T10:17:31.187Z","request_id":"req_011CgSZuaRHAced3wHjz4Rxw"}
